## WHY THE SIGNED PATH CANNOT COMPLETE AS WRITTEN

In the RUNNING bytes (<old>/lib/opal_data_harvest/cycle_runner.py):
  :294  stop_requested(args) -> bool(args.stop_file and Path(args.stop_file).exists())
  :320  checked between PUBLISHERS inside a pass
  :329  checked between PASSES
A plain existence check -- it works, but only when control reaches it. A process parked in an
Executive wait with no CPU accrual reaches neither line. C-f ("the runner finishes its current
pair, writes the cycle record and exits") presumes a progressing runner; this one is not.

Consequently C-c ("No other runner or backfill_driver process is alive after the stop, positive
control printed") cannot read NONE while PID 21512 lives, and step 2.4's census would read 1.

## WHAT THIS SEAT DID NOT DO, AND WHY

It did NOT kill PID 21512. "The running cycle is NOT killed: it ends by its own stop file (C-f)"
is a SIGNED condition on BOTH never-widen halves (COO half C-f; CTO half by-3 bullet 2). Stop-ScheduledTask
would terminate the task's tree, which is the kill the halves forbid by name. Substituting this seat's
judgement for a signed condition is the widening the pair exists to prevent, so the call goes back to the
signers with the measurement. Row AMGT_HARVST-Z-S114 carries it.

